nmso-para-margin-right:0in;\r\nmso-para-margin-bottom:10.0pt;\r\nmso-para-margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;\r\ntext-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:115%;\r\nmso-pagination:widow-orphan;\r\nfont-size:10.0pt;\r\nfont-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;\r\nmso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-hansi-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:\"Times New Roman\";}\r\n</style>\r\n<![endif]-->\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://www.tari.go.tz/ad/centres/edit/1\" target=\"_blank\">Organization Contact</a> </p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">. Box 5088 Tanga</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">. Telephone No. +255737374076</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;\r\ntext-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ascii-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-hansi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri\">. email: cdmlingano@tari.go.tz</span></p>','publish',9,1,'2020-11-21 00:00:00',NULL),(11,'TARI Dakawa','tari-dakawa',0,'<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(156, 0, 255); font-weight: bold;\">Establishment</span><span style=\"color: rgb(112, 48, 160);\"><o:p></o:p></span></span></i></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\">The Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI) Dakawa Centre was\r\nestablished in 1984 by a joint effort of the government of the United Republic of\r\nTanzania and the Government of the Democratic People\'s Republic of Korea; by then called <b>Chollima Agro-Scientific Research Centre. </b>Until today, the centre is famously known by the natives as<b>&nbsp;\'<i>Chollima\'.</i></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\">The centre is located at Dakawa in Mvomero District, about 45 kilometres from Morogoro Municipality, 3km from Morogoro - Dodoma main road, at -6.413789193601474, 37.53537143137759.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"Segoe UI Light, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">After the inception of TARI in 2018, the centre has been mandated to develop and disseminate result-based research outputs on the rice crop. Moreover, it deals with maize and horticultural crops in collaboration with other TARI centres so as to increase farm production and productivity in both lowland and medium-altitude areas of Tanzania Mainland.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; color: rgb(156, 0, 255);\">The vision of the centre</span></i><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\">The centre is envisioned <b>to become the rice\r\ncentre of excellence in the eastern, central and southern African regions.</b><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(156, 0, 255); font-weight: bold;\">The mission of the centre</span><span style=\"color: rgb(112, 48, 160);\"><o:p></o:p></span></span></i></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\">TARI Dakawa is commissioned to develop and disseminate\r\nresults-based- research outputs on rice leading to efficient and resilient\r\nfarming systems that protect or enhance farmer productivity, improve\r\nnutrition and raise net income while reducing reliance on pesticides and\r\nfertilizers and contribute to efficient farming that protect or enhance natural\r\nresources.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(156, 0, 255);\"><b><i>Management history</i></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\">Since its launch, the centre has been under the following administrative regimes:</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n</p><table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"border: none;\">\r\n <tbody><tr>\r\n  <td width=\"37\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:28.1pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  mso-border-alt:solid windowtext .5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\n  150%\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Trebuchet MS&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">SN<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.45pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-left:none;mso-border-left-alt:solid windowtext .5pt;mso-border-alt:\r\n  solid windowtext .5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\n  150%\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Trebuchet MS&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">NAME<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"180\" valign=\"top\"