pan><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td style=\\\"background-color:#ffffff; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:16px; vertical-align:top; width:306px\\\">\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p style=\\\"text-align:justify !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-size:15px !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif !important\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#212121 !important\\\">TARI Makutupora (Dodoma)<\\/span><\\/span><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td style=\\\"background-color:#ffffff; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:16px; vertical-align:top; width:437px\\\">\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p style=\\\"text-align:justify !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-size:15px !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif !important\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#212121 !important\\\">Grapes<\\/span><\\/span><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td style=\\\"background-color:#ffffff; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:17px; vertical-align:top; width:306px\\\">\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p style=\\\"text-align:justify !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-size:15px !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif !important\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#212121 !important\\\">TARI Kihinga (Kigoma)<\\/span><\\/span><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td style=\\\"background-color:#ffffff; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:17px; vertical-align:top; width:437px\\\">\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p style=\\\"text-align:justify !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-size:15px !important\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif !important\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#212121 !important\\\">Oil palm<\\/span><\\/span><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\",\"slug\":\"who-we-are\",\"status\":1,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-09T16:16:36.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-12T10:02:02.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:08:12','2025-06-28 04:08:12'),(625,6,'Page','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/pages/107','{\"id\":107,\"title_sw\":\"Mission and Vision\",\"title_en\":\"Mission and Vision\",\"has_sidebar\":\"1\",\"content_sw\":\"<p>\\ud83c\\udf1f <strong>Vision<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>To be the <strong>Institute of Excellence<\\/strong> for agricultural research in Tanzania and beyond.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\ude80 <strong>Mission<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>To <strong>generate and promote the application of knowledge, innovations, and agricultural technologies<\\/strong> as catalysts for change&mdash;driving agricultural productivity, food and nutrition security, sustainable farming systems, and economic growth. TARI works in close collaboration with national and international stakeholders to ensure inclusive and impactful research outcomes.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udca1 <strong>Our Goal<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>To contribute to <strong>increased agricultural productivity<\\/strong> by developing and deploying improved agricultural knowledge and technologies through an <strong>innovation systems approach<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udd1d <strong>Core Values<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>At TARI, our work is guided by a strong foundation of values that shape our culture and commitment to excellence:<\\/p>\",\"content_en\":\"<p><!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udf1f <strong>Vision<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>To be the <strong>Institute of Excellence<\\/strong> for agricultural research in Tanzania and beyond.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\ude80 <strong>Mission<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>To <strong>generate and promote the application of knowledge, innovations, and agricultural technologies<\\/strong> as catalysts for change&mdash;driving agricultural productivity, food and nutrition security, sustainable farming systems, and economic growth. TARI works in close collaboration with national and international stakeholders to ensure inclusive and impactful research outcomes.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udca1 <strong>Our Goal<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>To contribute to <strong>increased agricultural productivity<\\/strong> by developing and deploying improved agricultural knowledge and technologies through an <strong>innovation systems approach<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udd1d <strong>Core Values<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>At TARI, our work is guided by a strong foundation of values that shape our culture and commitment to excellence:<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\",\"slug\":\"mission-and-vision\",\"status\":1,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-12T10:50:52.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-12T10:50:52.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:11:33','2025-06-28 04:11:33'),(626,6,'Page','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/pages/108','{\"id\":108,\"title_sw\":\"What we Do\",\"title_en\":\"What we Do\",\"has_sidebar\":\"1\",\"content_sw\":\"<p>At the <strong>Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI)<\\/strong>, we are dedicated to transforming agriculture through science, innovation, and collaboration. Our work spans the entire agricultural value chain&mdash;from research and development to technology dissemination and farmer support&mdash;ensuring that our efforts lead to real-world impact.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udd2c <strong>Research &amp; Innovation<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>We conduct cutting-edge research to develop <strong>technologies, innovations, and management practices (TIMPs)<\\/strong> that address the evolving needs of farmers, agribusinesses, and policymakers. Our research focuses on:<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n\\t<li>Crop improvement and breeding for higher yields and resilience<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Soil fertility and sustainable land management<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Integrated pest and disease management<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Climate-smart agriculture and environmental sustainability<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Agricultural mechanization and digital technologies<!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DStartFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DEndFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udf31 <strong>Technology Development &amp; Dissemination<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI plays a central role in translating research into practice. We develop and promote <strong>farmer-friendly technologies<\\/strong> that enhance productivity, reduce risks, and improve livelihoods. Through field demonstrations, training sessions, and partnerships with extension services, we ensure that innovations reach the people who need them most.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udd1d <strong>Stakeholder Engagement<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>We work closely with a wide range of stakeholders&mdash;including farmers, researchers, extension agents, private sector actors, NGOs, and international partners&mdash;to co-create solutions and foster inclusive agricultural development. Our participatory approach ensures that research is <strong>demand-driven and locally relevant<\\/strong>.<!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DStartFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DEndFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udded <strong>Policy Support &amp; Advisory Services<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI provides evidence-based recommendations to inform national agricultural policies and strategies. Our data and insights help shape decisions that promote food security, economic growth, and environmental resilience.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udfe2 <strong>National Research Coordination<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>As the coordinating body for the <strong>National Agricultural Research System (NARS)<\\/strong>, TARI oversees and harmonizes research efforts across public and private institutions in Tanzania. We ensure that research activities are aligned with national priorities and contribute to the broader goals of sustainable development.<\\/p>\",\"content_en\":\"<p><!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>At the <strong>Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI)<\\/strong>, we are dedicated to transforming agriculture through science, innovation, and collaboration. Our work spans the entire agricultural value chain&mdash;from research and development to technology dissemination and farmer support&mdash;ensuring that our efforts lead to real-world impact.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udd2c <strong>Research &amp; Innovation<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>We conduct cutting-edge research to develop <strong>technologies, innovations, and management practices (TIMPs)<\\/strong> that address the evolving needs of farmers, agribusinesses, and policymakers. Our research focuses on:<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n\\t<li>Crop improvement and breeding for higher yields and resilience<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Soil fertility and sustainable land management<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Integrated pest and disease management<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Climate-smart agriculture and environmental sustainability<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Agricultural mechanization and digital technologies<!--StartFragment --><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udf31 <strong>Technology Development &amp; Dissemination<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI plays a central role in translating research into practice. We develop and promote <strong>farmer-friendly technologies<\\/strong> that enhance productivity, reduce risks, and improve livelihoods. Through field demonstrations, training sessions, and partnerships with extension services, we ensure that innovations reach the people who need them most.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udd1d <strong>Stakeholder Engagement<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>We work closely with a wide range of stakeholders&mdash;including farmers, researchers, extension agents, private sector actors, NGOs, and international partners&mdash;to co-create solutions and foster inclusive agricultural development. Our participatory approach ensures that research is <strong>demand-driven and locally relevant<\\/strong>.<!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udded <strong>Policy Support &amp; Advisory Services<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI provides evidence-based recommendations to inform national agricultural policies and strategies. Our data and insights help shape decisions that promote food security, economic growth, and environmental resilience.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udfe2 <strong>National Research Coordination<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>As the coordinating body for the <strong>National Agricultural Research System (NARS)<\\/strong>, TARI oversees and harmonizes research efforts across public and private institutions in Tanzania. We ensure that research activities are aligned with national priorities and contribute to the broader goals of sustainable development.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\",\"slug\":\"what-we-do\",\"status\":1,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-12T10:54:06.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-12T10:54:06.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:14:43','2025-06-28 04:14:43'),(627,6,'Page','destroy','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/pages/157','{\"id\":157,\"title_sw\":\"What we Do\",\"title_en\":\"What we Do\",\"has_sidebar\":1,\"content_sw\":\"<p>What we Do<\\/p>\",\"content_en\":\"<p>What we Do<\\/p>\",\"slug\":\"what-we-do-2\",\"status\":1,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-13T10:53:59.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-13T10:53:59.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:15:22','2025-06-28 04:15:22'),(628,6,'MenuItem','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/menu-items/281','{\"id\":281,\"title_sw\":\"What we Do\",\"title_en\":\"What we Do\",\"status\":1,\"menu_id\":\"8\",\"url\":\"pages\\/what-we-do\",\"url_external\":null,\"link\":\"1\",\"parent\":243,\"position\":3,\"has_sidebar\":0,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-09T13:11:10.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-19T09:58:26.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:15:59','2025-06-28 04:15:59'),(629,6,'Page','store','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/pages','{\"title_en\":\"Board of Directors\",\"title_sw\":\"Bodi Ya Wakurugenzi\",\"has_sidebar\":\"1\",\"content_en\":\"<p><!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udfdb\\ufe0f<strong> Board of Directors<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>The <strong>Board of Directors<\\/strong> provides strategic leadership, governance, and oversight for the Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI). Entrusted with ensuring accountability and institutional excellence, the Board plays a critical role in guiding TARI&rsquo;s mission and long-term vision.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udccc <strong>Composition<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>The TARI Board of Directors is composed of a <strong>Chairperson and 10 members<\\/strong>, representing a diverse range of expertise in agriculture, research, policy, and public service.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\uddd3\\ufe0f <strong>Tenure &amp; Meetings<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>The inaugural Board was officially inaugurated in <strong>July 2018<\\/strong>, with members appointed to serve a <strong>three-year term<\\/strong>. The Board convenes <strong>quarterly<\\/strong> to:<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n\\t<li>Review institutional progress and performance<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Provide strategic direction and policy guidance<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Approve key plans, budgets, and initiatives<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<!--EndFragment -->\\r\\n<\\/ul>\",\"content_sw\":\"<p><!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DStartFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udfdb\\ufe0f<strong> Board of Directors<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>The <strong>Board of Directors<\\/strong> provides strategic leadership, governance, and oversight for the Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI). Entrusted with ensuring accountability and institutional excellence, the Board plays a critical role in guiding TARI&rsquo;s mission and long-term vision.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udccc <strong>Composition<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>The TARI Board of Directors is composed of a <strong>Chairperson and 10 members<\\/strong>, representing a diverse range of expertise in agriculture, research, policy, and public service.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\uddd3\\ufe0f <strong>Tenure &amp; Meetings<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>The inaugural Board was officially inaugurated in <strong>July 2018<\\/strong>, with members appointed to serve a <strong>three-year term<\\/strong>. The Board convenes <strong>quarterly<\\/strong> to:<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n\\t<li>Review institutional progress and performance<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Provide strategic direction and policy guidance<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li>Approve key plans, budgets, and initiatives<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DEndFragment%20%2D%2D%3E-->\\r\\n<\\/ul>\",\"slug\":\"board-of-directors\"}','2025-06-28 04:21:38','2025-06-28 04:21:38'),(630,6,'MenuItem','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/menu-items/283','{\"id\":283,\"title_sw\":\"Bodi Ya Wakurugenzi\",\"title_en\":\"Board of Directors\",\"status\":1,\"menu_id\":\"8\",\"url\":\"pages\\/board-of-directors\",\"url_external\":null,\"link\":\"1\",\"parent\":243,\"position\":5,\"has_sidebar\":0,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-09T13:12:23.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-28T07:20:08.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:22:13','2025-06-28 04:22:13'),(631,6,'Page','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/pages/109','{\"id\":109,\"title_sw\":\"Organization Structure\",\"title_en\":\"Organization Structure\",\"has_sidebar\":\"1\",\"content_sw\":\"<p>The <strong>Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI)<\\/strong> is structured to ensure efficient coordination, accountability, and delivery of its national research mandate. The organizational framework supports both centralized leadership and decentralized operations across the country.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udfdb\\ufe0f <strong>Governance and Oversight<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>At the apex of the structure is the <strong>Board of Directors<\\/strong>, which provides strategic oversight, policy direction, and institutional governance. The Board ensures that TARI&rsquo;s operations align with national agricultural priorities and uphold standards of excellence and transparency.<!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DStartFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DEndFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udc64<strong> Executive Leadership<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI is led by the <strong>Director General<\\/strong>, who is responsible for the overall management and administration of the Institute. The Director General oversees the implementation of research programs, institutional development, and stakeholder engagement.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\uddea Research Centres and Sub-Centres<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI operates through a network of <strong>9 main research centres<\\/strong> and <strong>8 sub-centres<\\/strong>, strategically located across Tanzania to address region-specific agricultural challenges.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Main Centres<\\/strong> are led by <strong>Centre Directors<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Sub-Centres<\\/strong> are led by <strong>Centre Managers<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>This decentralized model enhances responsiveness, relevance, and farmer engagement across diverse agro-ecological zones.<!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DStartFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DEndFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udded <strong>Functional Structure<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI&rsquo;s operations are organized into three main <strong>Departments<\\/strong>, supported by specialized <strong>Units<\\/strong> that provide technical and administrative services:<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udcda <strong>Departments<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Research and Innovation<\\/strong><br \\/>\\r\\n\\tOversees the planning, execution, and evaluation of agricultural research programs across all centres.<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Technology Transfer and Partnerships<\\/strong><br \\/>\\r\\n\\tFacilitates the dissemination of research outputs, farmer training, and collaboration with stakeholders.<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Administration and Human Resource Management (HRM)<\\/strong><br \\/>\\r\\n\\tManages institutional support services, staffing, and organizational development<!--{C}%3C!%2D%2DStartFragment%20%2D%2D%3E--><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udee0\\ufe0f <strong>Support Units<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<table>\\r\\n\\t<thead>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<th>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Unit<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/th>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<th>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Key Responsibilities<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/th>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t<\\/thead>\\r\\n\\t<tbody>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Planning, Monitoring &amp; Evaluation&nbsp;and Statistics (PME)<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Coordinates the preparation, implementation, and evaluation of institutional plans, budgets and statistical analysis. Prepares budget speeches, annual economic reports, performance assessments, and integrates TARI&rsquo;s plans into national budgeting processes.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Finance and Accounts<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Manages financial operations, including payments, revenue collection, financial reporting, and audit coordination. Ensures compliance with financial regulations.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Internal Audit<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Provides advisory services on resource management, conducts audits, ensures compliance with financial procedures, and evaluates development project performance.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Procurement Management<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Oversees procurement, storage, and supply of goods and services. Ensures adherence to the Public Procurement Act, develops procurement plans, and supports logistical needs.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>ICT <\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Provides ICT support . Implements e-Government policies, maintains software and hardware, manages LAN\\/WAN communication, and promotes ICT for improved service delivery.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Legal Services<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Offers legal expertise on contracts, agreements, and legislation. Drafts legal documents, liaises with government legal bodies, and manages litigation and court decisions.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\",\"content_en\":\"<p><!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>The <strong>Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI)<\\/strong> is structured to ensure efficient coordination, accountability, and delivery of its national research mandate. The organizational framework supports both centralized leadership and decentralized operations across the country.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83c\\udfdb\\ufe0f <strong>Governance and Oversight<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>At the apex of the structure is the <strong>Board of Directors<\\/strong>, which provides strategic oversight, policy direction, and institutional governance. The Board ensures that TARI&rsquo;s operations align with national agricultural priorities and uphold standards of excellence and transparency.<!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udc64<strong> Executive Leadership<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI is led by the <strong>Director General<\\/strong>, who is responsible for the overall management and administration of the Institute. The Director General oversees the implementation of research programs, institutional development, and stakeholder engagement.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\uddea Research Centres and Sub-Centres<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI operates through a network of <strong>9 main research centres<\\/strong> and <strong>8 sub-centres<\\/strong>, strategically located across Tanzania to address region-specific agricultural challenges.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Main Centres<\\/strong> are led by <strong>Centre Directors<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Sub-Centres<\\/strong> are led by <strong>Centre Managers<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>This decentralized model enhances responsiveness, relevance, and farmer engagement across diverse agro-ecological zones.<!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83e\\udded <strong>Functional Structure<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>TARI&rsquo;s operations are organized into three main <strong>Departments<\\/strong>, supported by specialized <strong>Units<\\/strong> that provide technical and administrative services:<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udcda <strong>Departments<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Research and Innovation<\\/strong><br \\/>\\r\\n\\tOversees the planning, execution, and evaluation of agricultural research programs across all centres.<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Technology Transfer and Partnerships<\\/strong><br \\/>\\r\\n\\tFacilitates the dissemination of research outputs, farmer training, and collaboration with stakeholders.<\\/li>\\r\\n\\t<li><strong>Administration and Human Resource Management (HRM)<\\/strong><br \\/>\\r\\n\\tManages institutional support services, staffing, and organizational development<!--StartFragment --><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>\\ud83d\\udee0\\ufe0f <strong>Support Units<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<table>\\r\\n\\t<thead>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<th>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Unit<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/th>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<th>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Key Responsibilities<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/th>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t<\\/thead>\\r\\n\\t<tbody>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Planning, Monitoring &amp; Evaluation&nbsp;and Statistics (PME)<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Coordinates the preparation, implementation, and evaluation of institutional plans, budgets and statistical analysis. Prepares budget speeches, annual economic reports, performance assessments, and integrates TARI&rsquo;s plans into national budgeting processes.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Finance and Accounts<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Manages financial operations, including payments, revenue collection, financial reporting, and audit coordination. Ensures compliance with financial regulations.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Internal Audit<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Provides advisory services on resource management, conducts audits, ensures compliance with financial procedures, and evaluates development project performance.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Procurement Management<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Oversees procurement, storage, and supply of goods and services. Ensures adherence to the Public Procurement Act, develops procurement plans, and supports logistical needs.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>ICT <\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Provides ICT support . Implements e-Government policies, maintains software and hardware, manages LAN\\/WAN communication, and promotes ICT for improved service delivery.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><strong>Legal Services<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Offers legal expertise on contracts, agreements, and legislation. Drafts legal documents, liaises with government legal bodies, and manages litigation and court decisions.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\r\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\r\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\",\"slug\":\"organization-structure\",\"status\":1,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-12T10:54:34.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-12T10:54:34.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:36:15','2025-06-28 04:36:15'),(632,6,'AdministrationCategories','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/administration_categories/2','{\"id\":2,\"title_sw\":\"Management Team\",\"title_en\":\"Management Team\",\"summary_sw\":\"The Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI) is managed by a team of experienced professionals committed to advancing agricultural research and innovation for national development. The management team is responsible for the day-to-day operations of the Institute, ensuring that strategic goals are effectively implemented and aligned with national agricultural priorities.\\r\\n\\ud83e\\udded Executive Leadership\\r\\n- Director General\\r\\nThe Director General serves as the Chief Executive Officer of the Institute, providing overall leadership, strategic direction, and institutional representation. The Director General oversees the implementation of research programs, resource mobilization, stakeholder engagement, and performance monitoring across all TARI centres.\\r\\n- Directors of Departments\\r\\nTARI\\u2019s core functions are managed through three main departments, each led by a Director:\\r\\n- Director of Research and Innovation \\u2013 Oversees the planning, coordination, and quality assurance of all research activities.\\r\\n- Director of Technology Transfer and Partnerships \\u2013 Leads the dissemination of research outputs, stakeholder collaboration, and farmer outreach.\\r\\n- Director of Administration and Human Resource Management \\u2013 Manages institutional support services, staffing, and organizational development\\r\\n\\ud83c\\udfe2 Centre Leadership\\r\\n- Centre Directors\\r\\nEach of TARI\\u2019s 9 main research centres is led by a Centre Director, who is responsible for coordinating research programs, managing staff, and ensuring the relevance and impact of research activities in their respective regions.\\r\\n- Centre Managers\\r\\nThe 8 sub-centres are led by Centre Managers, who support localized research and extension services, working closely with farmers and regional stakeholders.\\r\\n\\ud83d\\udd27 Technical and Support Units\\r\\nTARI\\u2019s management is supported by heads of specialized units who provide technical expertise and operational support in areas such as:\\r\\n- Planning, Monitoring & Evaluation\\r\\n- Finance and Accounts\\r\\n- Procurement Management\\r\\n- Internal Audit\\r\\n- ICT and Statistics\\r\\n- Legal Services\\r\\n\\r\\nTogether, this integrated management structure ensures that TARI remains responsive, innovative, and accountable in delivering agricultural solutions that benefit farmers, policymakers, and the broader Tanzanian economy.\",\"summary_en\":\"The Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI) is managed by a team of experienced professionals committed to advancing agricultural research and innovation for national development. The management team is responsible for the day-to-day operations of the Institute, ensuring that strategic goals are effectively implemented and aligned with national agricultural priorities.\\r\\n\\ud83e\\udded Executive Leadership\\r\\n- Director General\\r\\nThe Director General serves as the Chief Executive Officer of the Institute, providing overall leadership, strategic direction, and institutional representation. The Director General oversees the implementation of research programs, resource mobilization, stakeholder engagement, and performance monitoring across all TARI centres.\\r\\n- Directors of Departments\\r\\nTARI\\u2019s core functions are managed through three main departments, each led by a Director:\\r\\n- Director of Research and Innovation \\u2013 Oversees the planning, coordination, and quality assurance of all research activities.\\r\\n- Director of Technology Transfer and Partnerships \\u2013 Leads the dissemination of research outputs, stakeholder collaboration, and farmer outreach.\\r\\n- Director of Administration and Human Resource Management \\u2013 Manages institutional support services, staffing, and organizational development\\r\\n\\ud83c\\udfe2 Centre Leadership\\r\\n- Centre Directors\\r\\nEach of TARI\\u2019s 9 main research centres is led by a Centre Director, who is responsible for coordinating research programs, managing staff, and ensuring the relevance and impact of research activities in their respective regions.\\r\\n- Centre Managers\\r\\nThe 8 sub-centres are led by Centre Managers, who support localized research and extension services, working closely with farmers and regional stakeholders.\\r\\n\\ud83d\\udd27 Technical and Support Units\\r\\nTARI\\u2019s management is supported by heads of specialized units who provide technical expertise and operational support in areas such as:\\r\\n- Planning, Monitoring & Evaluation\\r\\n- Finance and Accounts\\r\\n- Procurement Management\\r\\n- Internal Audit\\r\\n- ICT and Statistics\\r\\n- Legal Services\\r\\n\\r\\nTogether, this integrated management structure ensures that TARI remains responsive, innovative, and accountable in delivering agricultural solutions that benefit farmers, policymakers, and the broader Tanzanian economy.\",\"featured\":\"1\",\"slug\":\"administration\",\"content\":null,\"active\":1,\"created_at\":\"2022-08-17T11:21:41.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2022-10-15T15:35:38.000000Z\",\"center_id\":null}','2025-06-28 04:40:51','2025-06-28 04:40:51'),(633,6,'AdministrationCategories','store','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/administration_categories','{\"title_sw\":\"Watumishi\",\"title_en\":\"Staff\",\"summary_sw\":\"aa\",\"summary_en\":\"a\",\"featured\":\"0\",\"slug\":\"staff\"}','2025-06-28 04:49:12','2025-06-28 04:49:12'),(634,6,'AdministrationCategories','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/administration_categories/7','{\"id\":7,\"title_sw\":\"Watumishi\",\"title_en\":\"Staff\",\"summary_sw\":\"\\ud83d\\udc69\\u200d\\ud83d\\udd2c Our Staff\\r\\nThe strength of the Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI) lies in its dedicated and diverse team of professionals who drive the Institute\\u2019s mission forward. Our staff are the backbone of agricultural innovation in Tanzania\\u2014bringing together scientific expertise, technical skills, and a deep commitment to improving the livelihoods of farmers and communities across the country.\\r\\n\\ud83d\\udc65 Who We Are\\r\\nTARI employs a multidisciplinary team of experts, including:\\r\\n- Agricultural researchers and scientists specializing in crop improvement, soil science, plant protection, biotechnology, and climate-smart agriculture\\r\\n- Extension specialists and technology transfer officers who bridge the gap between research and farmers\\r\\n- Engineers and technicians supporting agricultural mechanization and infrastructure\\r\\n- Administrative and support staff ensuring smooth operations across all centres\\r\\n- Finance, procurement, ICT, legal, and planning professionals who provide essential institutional services\\r\\n\\ud83c\\udf0d Nationwide Presence\\r\\nWith staff stationed at 9 main research centres and 8 sub-centres across Tanzania, TARI maintains a strong presence in all major agro-ecological zones. This decentralized staffing model allows for:\\r\\n- Region-specific research and innovation\\r\\n- Close collaboration with local farmers and stakeholders\\r\\n- Rapid response to emerging agricultural challenges\\r\\n\\ud83d\\udcda Capacity Building and Development\\r\\nTARI is committed to continuous professional development. We invest in:\\r\\n- Training and capacity building for staff at all levels\\r\\n- Collaborative research programs with national and international institutions\\r\\n- Knowledge exchange platforms to foster innovation and learning\\r\\n\\ud83e\\udd1d A Culture of Excellence\\r\\nOur staff embody TARI\\u2019s core values of professionalism, teamwork, integrity, and inclusiveness. Through their dedication and expertise, TARI continues to be a trusted leader in agricultural research and a catalyst for sustainable development in Tanzania and beyond.\",\"summary_en\":\"\\ud83d\\udc69\\u200d\\ud83d\\udd2c Our Staff\\r\\nThe strength of the Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI) lies in its dedicated and diverse team of professionals who drive the Institute\\u2019s mission forward. Our staff are the backbone of agricultural innovation in Tanzania\\u2014bringing together scientific expertise, technical skills, and a deep commitment to improving the livelihoods of farmers and communities across the country.\\r\\n\\ud83d\\udc65 Who We Are\\r\\nTARI employs a multidisciplinary team of experts, including:\\r\\n- Agricultural researchers and scientists specializing in crop improvement, soil science, plant protection, biotechnology, and climate-smart agriculture\\r\\n- Extension specialists and technology transfer officers who bridge the gap between research and farmers\\r\\n- Engineers and technicians supporting agricultural mechanization and infrastructure\\r\\n- Administrative and support staff ensuring smooth operations across all centres\\r\\n- Finance, procurement, ICT, legal, and planning professionals who provide essential institutional services\\r\\n\\ud83c\\udf0d Nationwide Presence\\r\\nWith staff stationed at 9 main research centres and 8 sub-centres across Tanzania, TARI maintains a strong presence in all major agro-ecological zones. This decentralized staffing model allows for:\\r\\n- Region-specific research and innovation\\r\\n- Close collaboration with local farmers and stakeholders\\r\\n- Rapid response to emerging agricultural challenges\\r\\n\\ud83d\\udcda Capacity Building and Development\\r\\nTARI is committed to continuous professional development. We invest in:\\r\\n- Training and capacity building for staff at all levels\\r\\n- Collaborative research programs with national and international institutions\\r\\n- Knowledge exchange platforms to foster innovation and learning\\r\\n\\ud83e\\udd1d A Culture of Excellence\\r\\nOur staff embody TARI\\u2019s core values of professionalism, teamwork, integrity, and inclusiveness. Through their dedication and expertise, TARI continues to be a trusted leader in agricultural research and a catalyst for sustainable development in Tanzania and beyond.\",\"featured\":\"0\",\"slug\":\"staff\",\"content\":null,\"active\":1,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-28T07:49:12.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-28T07:49:12.000000Z\",\"center_id\":null}','2025-06-28 04:50:51','2025-06-28 04:50:51'),(635,6,'MenuItem','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/menu-items/285','{\"id\":285,\"title_sw\":\"Watumishi wa Taasisi\",\"title_en\":\"Staff\",\"status\":1,\"menu_id\":\"8\",\"url\":\"administration\\/staff\",\"url_external\":null,\"link\":\"1\",\"parent\":243,\"position\":7,\"has_sidebar\":0,\"created_at\":\"2025-06-09T13:14:44.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-06-28T07:20:08.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:51:28','2025-06-28 04:51:28'),(636,6,'WelcomeNote','update','154.74.190.0','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/welcome/2','{\"id\":2,\"summary_en\":\"The Management of the National Prosecutions Office, would like to invite all stakeholders to the website of the National Prosecution services.\",\"summary_sw\":\"Uongozi na Menejimenti nzima pamoja na Wafanyakazi wa Ofisi ya Taifa ya Mashtaka, wanawakaribisha  wadau wote ndani na nje ya nchi kutembelea Tovuti ya ofisi kwa ajili ya kupata na kujua juu ya taarifa mbalimbali ambazo ofisi inashughulika nayo. karibuni \",\"content_sw\":\"<p><!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>Welcome to the <strong>Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI)<\\/strong> &mdash; the national hub of agricultural innovation, research excellence, and farmer-focused solutions.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>At TARI, we believe that agriculture is the backbone of Tanzania&rsquo;s economy and the key to achieving food security, environmental sustainability, and inclusive economic growth. Our dedicated team of scientists, researchers, technicians, and support staff work tirelessly across the country to develop and deliver cutting-edge technologies and practices that empower farmers and transform rural livelihoods.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>With a strong foundation in science and a deep commitment to service, we are proud to lead the way in agricultural research and development. Whether you&#39;re a farmer, policymaker, development partner, or researcher, we invite you to explore our work, connect with our experts, and join us in building a more resilient and productive agricultural sector for Tanzania and beyond.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>Together, let&rsquo;s cultivate innovation for a better tomorrow.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\",\"content_en\":\"<p><!--StartFragment --><\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>Welcome to the <strong>Tanzania Agricultural Research Institute (TARI)<\\/strong> &mdash; the national hub of agricultural innovation, research excellence, and farmer-focused solutions.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>At TARI, we believe that agriculture is the backbone of Tanzania&rsquo;s economy and the key to achieving food security, environmental sustainability, and inclusive economic growth. Our dedicated team of scientists, researchers, technicians, and support staff work tirelessly across the country to develop and deliver cutting-edge technologies and practices that empower farmers and transform rural livelihoods.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>With a strong foundation in science and a deep commitment to service, we are proud to lead the way in agricultural research and development. Whether you&#39;re a farmer, policymaker, development partner, or researcher, we invite you to explore our work, connect with our experts, and join us in building a more resilient and productive agricultural sector for Tanzania and beyond.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>Together, let&rsquo;s cultivate innovation for a better tomorrow.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p><!--EndFragment --><\\/p>\",\"status\":\"1\",\"created_at\":\"2025-05-30T10:02:52.000000Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-05-30T17:02:52.000000Z\"}','2025-06-28 04:54:16','2025-06-28 04:54:16'),(637,6,'Announcement','update','196.45.128.114','http://demo81.eganet.go.tz/tari/cms/announcements/9','{\"id\":9,\"title_sw\":\"Research and Innovation meeting\",\"title_en\":\"Research and Innovation meeting\",\"content_sw\":\"<div class=\\\"bootstrap-tabs\\\" data-tab-set-title=\\\"Research and Innovation meeting\\\">\\r\\n<ul class=\\\"nav nav-tabs\\\" role=\\\"tablist\\\"><!-- add tabs here 